The waiter stands at my table.
He looks at his small notepad.
“That is eleven Euro eighty in total, please,” he says.
I open my wallet.
I take out a twenty Euro note.
I give him the money.
“Thirteen Euro, please,” I say.
The waiter smiles.
“Thank you very much,” he answers.
He gives me seven Euro back.
“Do you need the receipt?” he asks.
“No, thank you,” I answer.
I put my wallet into my backpack.
Then I stand up.
I put on my thick winter coat.
“Goodbye!” I say.
“Thank you, have a nice day!” the waiter calls.
I open the door.
I step back out into the cold Berlin air.
